    <div class="bio">
      <h3 class="bio-label">About the founder</h3>
      <p>Karthik S. is the Founder and Principal Consultant of Qualiber, bringing nearly two decades of experience in quality engineering, technical program management, and software delivery. With a career spanning Amazon and Apple, he combines deep technical expertise with experience leading complex, cross-functional programs at scale.</p>
      <p>Prior to founding Qualiber, Karthik led end-to-end quality and release strategy for Amazon’s reading platforms, serving more than 50 million users. During his four years at Amazon, he developed a GenAI-powered testing accelerator that reduced execution time by 50% and delivered $1.2 million in annual run-rate savings. He also took GenAI and agentic AI initiatives from pilot through production adoption and served as an Amazon Bar Raiser, contributing to hiring standards across the organisation.</p>
      <p>Previously, Karthik directed quality engineering and testing for Apple News, where his work included improving publisher-payout data accuracy and developing machine-learning-driven approaches to detect anomalies across analytics systems.</p>
      <p>Karthik’s experience across large-scale technology environments has reinforced a central principle behind his work: successful software delivery depends not only on technical capability, but also on effective coordination and evidence-based decision-making. He brings this perspective to Qualiber, where he is building an AI-powered decision platform designed to give engineering teams clearer, evidence-based insight into release readiness.</p>
      <p>Karthik holds an Executive MBA from the University of Chicago Booth School of Business and a Bachelor of Engineering in Electrical, Electronics and Communications Engineering from Anna University Chennai.</p>
    </div>
